      "scenario": "The adjacency rule masks quoted contents before classifying assignments, so x=\"$(false)\" and an expansion of an unset conditional variable are accepted between allocation and trap registration. They exit 1 before installing cleanup and leave the directory. The trap grammar also permits an additional uninitialized operand, which prevents rm from executing under set -u. Arithmetic/heredoc state is still line-local, so quoted and unquoted shifts spread over two lines hide a later mktemp. All five accepted cases leave TMPDIR nonempty and pass ShellCheck --severity=warning. Complete-gate tracked-script substitutions for command substitution in the gap and multiline arithmetic both return 0.",
